        "name": "USN-3968-2",
        "description": "USN-3968-1 fixed a vulnerability in Sudo. This update provides the corresponding update for Ubuntu 14.04 ESM.  Original advisory details:   It was discovered that Sudo did not properly parse the contents of  /proc/[pid]/stat when attempting to determine its controlling tty. A local  attacker in some configurations could possibly use this to overwrite any  file on the filesystem, bypassing intended permissions. (CVE-2017-1000368)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2017-1000368"
        ]
      },
